	"bugClass": {
		"id": "actor-identity-literal-mismatch",
		"title": "Canary verdict rejects valid answers from client-specific actors",
		"cause": "A verdict or acceptance check compares an actor field against one hard-coded identity even though different client write paths record different actor strings or omit the field and rely on a default. Test fakes that omit actor metadata can conceal the mismatch.",
		"criteria": "Classify another site when a verdict or acceptance check requires an exact actor identity and at least one valid client path writes a different identity or leaves it unset for a default. Separate client paths are sufficient independently. Include cases where test doubles omit or normalize actor metadata and therefore fail to represent production writes.",
